# Docked Filter Panel

Reference: lots page `src/app/(app)/lots/LotsWorkspace.tsx` (opens from **Filter** next to the page title).

When the user says **docked-filter-panel** (or docked filter), reuse this instead of a modal, dropdown, or inline filter bar.

## Chrome

- Starts **closed**. A page-title **Filter** button opens it.
- **Docked left**, width **30%**, slides over the list (does not shrink the table).
- Top edge is **below the white header + nav**, in the light gray (`bg-stone-50`) content area. Header stays visible.
- Overlay is **transparent** (click it to close). Panel has a **drop shadow** onto the page.
- Close with ×, overlay click, or Escape.
- Panel canvas is a cool muted tint so it reads apart from a details dock: `bg-slate-100` padding, inner card `rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 shadow-sm`, same headings and field chrome as the rest of the page. Details docks (`DockedPanel`) are a very light muted amber, fully opaque: `bg-[#eee8d3]` padding and a `bg-[#f8f5e8]` card with a `border-[#ddd5bb]` edge, so the white Fit List and boxes stand on it. Both cards carry `dock-panel`; `globals.css` keeps every input, select, and textarea inside them white. The lots page has its own aside and uses the same slate classes.
- `side="right"` is available but the default, and every current filter, is left.
- Footer: **Filter** (`Btn`) applies and **keeps the panel open**; **Reset** clears fields and the applied filter.

## Apply state

- Empty fields are ignored; filled fields combine with **AND**.
- Catalog fields use **Combo Box**. Text fields match contains (case-insensitive).
- Each editable control has an inner **×** on the right to clear that field only.
- While a filter is applied, the page button label is **Filtered** with a **semi-transparent red** background. Reset restores **Filter** and the normal white button.

## Fit List

- Filter the rows passed into the paged Fit List. Jump/select a row with Fit List `focusId` / `focusNonce` (tryLeave if a row is dirty in edit).
- Optional **Find** (←, `title="Find"`) inside a key field: if that record is in the **current filtered** list, page to it, select it, and **close** the panel. No match → panel stays open.

## Lots extras (this page only)

- Lot No filled → Article and Color # are **watermarks** (not inputs), parsed from the lot.
- Find matches **exact** lot number (case-insensitive) in the filtered list.
